From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t3code-customize <t3code-customize@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:49:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] feat(web): show each Claude skill load as its own
 timeline row

A Skill tool call was folded into the surrounding tool group, so a loaded
skill only showed up after expanding "Used N tools" and then its row, which
opened raw JSON.

Pull Skill calls out of the work group the way context compaction is, and
render them like the Claude Code CLI does: "Skill(name)" with the arguments,
and a status line below it ("Loading skill" with the activity shimmer,
"Successfully loaded skill", or "Failed to load skill"). The row has nothing
to expand and stays visible when a finished turn folds its work.
